  "Saved": "Salvato",
  "Give it a name": "Inserisci un nome",
  "A bit bigger, please — draw that one again.": "Un po' più grande, per favore — riprova.",
  "Straight lines are taken as scrolling. Draw a shape with a turn in it.": "Le linee rette valgono come scorrimento. Disegna una curva o un angolo.",
  "Got it. Again.": "Preso. Ancora una volta.",
  "Looks distinct from the other gestures. Save it.": "È ben distinto dagli altri gesti. Salvalo.",
  "Saved, but it can't be used with one finger: it isn't a closed shape": "Salvato, ma non usabile con un dito: non è una forma chiusa",
  "A cross is two quick diagonal strokes, which is exactly what two flicks look like while scrolling a feed or moving a map. With one finger it would go off by itself.": "Una croce assomiglia a due scorrimenti rapidi e si attiverebbe da sola con un dito.",
  "This is two straight lines with one corner. Ordinary drags, swipes between photos and the back gesture draw that shape all the time, so with one finger it would go off by itself.": "Due linee con un angolo assomigliano troppo ai normali gesti indietro.",
  "Part of this digit is an open line, and a scroll that curls at the end can look just like it. With one finger it would go off by itself.": "Parte di questa cifra è aperta e assomiglia a uno scorrimento curvo.",
  "A one-finger swipe is how every app scrolls.": "Scorrere con un dito serve per scorrere in tutte le app.",
  "This digit is an open line that doesn't end where it starts. A curved scroll or swipe in an app can draw the same shape, so with one finger it would go off by itself.": "Questa cifra non torna al punto iniziale e potrebbe scattare scorrendo.",
  "With one finger only closed shapes are allowed (one stroke that ends where it started), because ordinary scrolls and swipes never do that. This custom gesture isn't drawn that way.": "Con un dito sono ammesse solo forme chiuse (un tratto che torna all'inizio).",
